# Production build settings.
#
# Empty on purpose. nginx serves this build and proxies /api to the Node
# process on the same origin, so the API base must be the empty string — which
# also keeps the session cookies first-party.
#
# This file exists so that a plain `npm run build` is correct by default.
# Without it VITE_API_URL is undefined, api.js falls back to
# http://localhost:4000, and every request from a visitor's browser fails with
# "We could not reach the server" — a build that looks fine and is broken for
# everyone but the person who built it.
VITE_API_URL=
